.TH LEMONVOX 1 "November 2026" "LemonVox" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lemonvox \- speech dictation client for GNOME Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lemonvox
.RI [ --settings | --service | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
LemonVox captures speech after an explicit user action and sends it to a
separately running Lemonade or compatible transcription and chat server.
The server and models must be installed and configured separately.
The selected server may run locally or remotely.
Completed dictation is pasted at the current keyboard focus without sending
Enter. Copy remains available when paste cannot be dispatched.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --settings
Open the settings window.
.TP
.B --service
Run the session D-Bus service used by the desktop integration.
.TP
.B --version
Print version information and exit.
.SH DESKTOP SETUP
Use a GNOME 46 or 51 Wayland session. After installing, log out and back in, then
run the following as the desktop user:
.PP
.nf
  gnome-extensions enable lemonvox@itomek.com
.fi
.PP
Open LemonVox settings to configure the server and transcription and cleanup
models. The default dictation shortcut is Ctrl+Alt+Space; Ctrl+Super+Escape
cancels an active operation. The GNOME extension supplies global shortcuts
and the dictation indicator.
.SH FILES
User preferences are stored in the XDG configuration directory and are
retained when the package is removed.
.SH PRIVACY
Microphone capture starts only after a user action. Audio is sent to the
configured server. Server retention depends on that server's configuration.
Dictated content is not intended for diagnostic logs. Pasted or copied text
remains on the desktop clipboard according to its normal lifetime.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gnome-extensions (1)
.PP
https://github.com/itomek/lemonvox
